dzn: Keep command buffers' upload buffers mapped and reuse them

Every command buffer that needed upload memory, for dynamic uniform
buffer descriptors, buffer fills and updates, clears or triangle fans,
created a 4 MiB upload buffer, mapped and unmapped it for each use, and
released it when the command buffer was reset. Under WSL2 each of those
is a call into the host's graphics kernel, and an application recording
a new command buffer every frame paid for all of them every frame.

Map an upload buffer once, when it is created, and on reset keep up to
four of them for the command buffer's next recording, as the reset path's
TODO asked.

